 ],
 "literal": "In the dark backwater, as the sapphire-like flowers close, the pure waves / with foaming spray and drizzle, along with the mist enveloping, / with the caressing cold wind that came causing helplessness, / an unpleasant dwelling it will become, / for a few days, alas, in this small, good town!",
 "translation": "As the sapphire-blue flowers of the dark backwater close, the pure waves rise with foaming spray and drizzle. Enveloped by the mist and accompanied by the caressing cold wind that brings helplessness, staying in this small, good town will become highly unpleasant for a few days, alas!",
 "modern": "கரிய கழியில் உள்ள நீல நிற மலர்கள் குவியுமாறு, தூய அலைகளின் பொங்குகின்ற நீர்த்துளிகளோடு பனிமூட்டமும் சூழ்ந்து கொள்கிறது. செயலற்றுப் போகுமாறு வீசுகின்ற குளிர்ந்த காற்றோடு சேர்ந்து, இந்தச் சிறிய நல்ல ஊரில் தங்கியிருப்பது இன்னும் சில நாட்களுக்குத் துன்பம் தருவதாக அமையும்.",
 "explanation": "The friend speaks to the heroine (or within the hearing of the hero) during the onset of the cold season. She describes how the evening brings a cold wind, mist, and spray from the sea, causing the blue lily flowers in the backwater to close. This cold wind ('ūtai') is described as 'caressing' yet bringing a sense of helplessness ('kaiyaṟa') to those in separation. The friend laments that staying in this otherwise beautiful, small coastal town will become extremely painful for the next few days. Through these vivid images of the Neytal (coastal) landscape, she highlights the agony of separation and indirectly urges the hero to hasten the marriage.",
